                <head>77. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>In late 1964, Special Assistant to the President for National Security Affairs
                        McGeorge Bundy was advised of
                    information indicating that the Pakistani Government had a secret commitment
                    from China that established a significantly closer relationship between the two
                    countries than had been publicly acknowledged, although the details of such
                    commitment were not available to the United States Government.</p>
            </div>
